A man described finding himself in a group of twelve people (including himself) with the following characteristics:

a) Each person was not acquainted with six others but knew everyone else;

b) Each person belonged to a trio of mutually acquainted people;

c) Among those gathered, it was impossible to select four people who were all mutually acquainted;

d) It was also impossible to select four people who were all mutually unacquainted;

e) Each person was part of a trio of mutually unacquainted people;

f) Each person in the group could find someone among the people they did not know who had no common acquaintances within the group. 

Upon hearing this, Dr. Sharadek claimed that he had once encountered a society where conditions b), c), d), and e) were met, but each person knew exactly six others and had an acquaintance who could introduce them to everyone else.

Explain these situations.

Let \( n \) be an odd number greater than 1, and define the following:

\[
\begin{array}{l}
X_{0} = \left\{x_{1}^{(0)}, x_{2}^{(0)}, \cdots, x_{n}^{(0)}\right\} = \{1, 0, \cdots, 0, 1\}, \\
X_{k} = \left\{x_{1}^{(k)}, x_{2}^{(k)}, \cdots, x_{n}^{(k)}\right\}, \quad k = 1, 2, \cdots,
\end{array}
\]

where \( x_{i}^{(k)} = \begin{cases}
0 & \text{if } x_{i}^{(k-1)} = x_{i+1}^{(k-1)} \\
1 & \text{if } x_{i}^{(k-1)} \neq x_{i+1}^{(k-1)}
\end{cases}, \quad i = 1, 2, \cdots, n \). Here, \( x_{(n+1)}^{(k-1)} = x_{1}^{(k-1)} \).

Given that for \( m \in \mathbf{N}_{+} \) we have \( X_{m} = X_{0} \), prove that \( n \mid m \).

One mole of an ideal gas undergoes a closed cycle in which:

$1-2$ - isobaric process, where the volume increases by 4 times;

$2-3$ - isothermal process, where the pressure increases;

$3-1$ - process in which the gas is compressed according to the law $T=\gamma V^{2}$.

Determine by what factor the volume in state 3 exceeds the initial volume in state 1.
